==English==

===Etymology===
A diminutive of {{etyl|it}} [[Margherita]], and {{etyl|la}} and {{etyl|es}} [[Margarita]], all cognates of English [[Margaret]]. An Italian [[w:Rita of Cascia|Saint Rita]] was [[canonize]]d in 1900. The English name came into regular use in early twentieth century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|iːtə}}

